A big shout out to the volunteers at DevCon.

792
00:40:52.320 --> 00:40:56.990
DevCon is really made possible by the heartbeat

793
00:40:56.990 --> 00:40:59.470
of a lot of valuable volunteers

794
00:40:59.470 --> 00:41:01.950
that have been doing it on repeat.

795
00:41:01.950 --> 00:41:04.430
I myself have been volunteering for many events

796
00:41:04.430 --> 00:41:06.510
and a lot of the volunteers I've seen do it

797
00:41:06.510 --> 00:41:09.030
many times before and they'll keep doing it

798
00:41:09.030 --> 00:41:11.590
for more events around the world.

799
00:41:11.590 --> 00:41:15.550
So if you ever wanted an open door into Ethereum,

800
00:41:15.550 --> 00:41:18.910
I definitely recommend volunteering at any of the events.

801
00:41:18.910 --> 00:41:22.630
Open Source Orchestra is also completely run

802
00:41:22.630 --> 00:41:24.870
and supported by volunteers.

803
00:41:24.870 --> 00:41:26.750
We've been doing it with no funding

804
00:41:26.750 --> 00:41:30.830
and there's usually, yeah, no compensation

805
00:41:30.830 --> 00:41:32.270
that we're able to be distributing.

806
00:41:32.270 --> 00:41:35.990
So that's part of the idea in the Open Source Orchestra DAO

807
00:41:35.990 --> 00:41:38.430
is to see how we can actually rewrite some

808
00:41:38.430 --> 00:41:40.630
of those narratives that we actually have funding,

809
00:41:40.630 --> 00:41:43.310
that we can start accommodating more people.

810
00:41:43.310 --> 00:41:47.110
And I would love to continue the relationship

811
00:41:47.110 --> 00:41:50.350
of having it be a gift with the different events

812
00:41:50.350 --> 00:41:51.550
that have always hosted us,

813
00:41:51.550 --> 00:41:53.350
that it's more like we're sponsoring,

814
00:41:53.350 --> 00:41:56.470
that we're showing up and providing this experience.

815
00:41:56.510 --> 00:41:59.830
We're not depending on them to hire us or pay us

816
00:41:59.830 --> 00:42:02.550
or even set up all the production for us.

817
00:42:02.550 --> 00:42:06.990
Although, when you're plugging into the World Geo Center,

818
00:42:06.990 --> 00:42:10.110
you wanna be plugged into their main production

819
00:42:10.110 --> 00:42:13.590
and having a back line that is there waiting for you

820
00:42:13.590 --> 00:42:17.750
when you fly across the world, that's also very valuable.

821
00:42:17.750 --> 00:42:20.350
So it's the only way that this will be capable

822
00:42:20.350 --> 00:42:24.270
is if we're still having the relationship with the events,

823
00:42:25.230 --> 00:42:29.430
but as well as it just needs to have the strong essence

824
00:42:29.430 --> 00:42:30.790
that the community is the one

825
00:42:30.790 --> 00:42:33.270
that's putting gasoline in the fire

826
00:42:34.430 --> 00:42:40.100
and keeping things burning so that the fire stays warm

827
00:42:41.420 --> 00:42:44.340
and then we make the music and we get the dance

828
00:42:44.340 --> 00:42:48.420
and we get the rhythm going and then people gather

829
00:42:48.420 --> 00:42:51.460
like they gathered for the closing party of DEFCON

830
00:42:51.460 --> 00:42:58.280
and it just really, you know, it leaves you inspired.

831
00:42:58.600 --> 00:43:01.360
So that's the whole goal of the Open Source Orchestra

832
00:43:01.360 --> 00:43:04.960
is that we leave people inspired

833
00:43:04.960 --> 00:43:08.000
to wanna keep building, to keep participating

834
00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:13.000
and to keep connecting and unifying in this tech space

835
00:43:13.080 --> 00:43:17.160
that is much better shared when it's open sourced.

836
00:43:17.160 --> 00:43:19.560
And now that we can also put music out there

837
00:43:19.560 --> 00:43:20.720
in a similar narrative,

838
00:43:20.720 --> 00:43:22.280
I think that's kind of the message

839
00:43:22.280 --> 00:43:23.760
we're trying to put forth.

840
00:43:23.760 --> 00:43:28.860
So much love to all of you and thank you.

841
00:43:29.260 --> 00:43:33.300
Gonna send this to googlyeye to transcribe

842
00:43:33.300 --> 00:43:35.980
and then we'll be posting it live very soon

843
00:43:35.980 --> 00:43:41.280
and see you at Open Source Orchestra at Dal meet number five.

844
00:43:41.280 --> 00:43:45.890
Peace out, stop recording.

845
00:43:45.890 --> 00:43:46.730
Aloha.
